  "body": "Found while working #3679.\n\n## What happens\n\n`Rest::cut` takes the chords of every non-Rapid move. A feed dive that\nthe plunge depth law names (`PlungeTooDeep`, #3679) inserts its own\nchord into that set. A later move then reads the dive's column as\ncleared to the dive bottom:\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/plunge_depth.rs`, test\n  `a_feed_plunge_deeper_than_one_stepdown_below_uncut_stock_is_named`,\n  pins this: the re-entry plunge after the 18 mm dive reads the column\n  as cleared to Z -18 and stays clean.\n\nThe rest model is physically true: the dive removed that material,\nunsafely, but it did remove it. The question is whether a verifier\nshould treat an unsafe removal as a proven floor, or should exclude a\nnamed dive from the clearing set so the later laws speak against the\nstock that should still stand.\n\n## Expected\n\nA recorded decision: keep the current reading, or exclude over-deep\ndives from `Rest::cut`. Each answer gets its own pinning test.\n\n## Done means\n\nA `docs/decisions/` entry names the choice, and the verify tests pin\nthe chosen reading.\n\n## Notes\n\n- #3678 fixes the generator dives. After it, no tab window dive is\n  over-deep, so the question matters only for hand-built or imported\n  programs.\n",
